{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"agent_message","text":"Disassembly shows the exact cause: GCC evaluates `c2Dot` into `y-product + x-product`, with the second product’s operands reversed, while Rust emitted `x-product + y-product`. I’m matching that emitted C order explicitly; this is behaviorally identical for normal numbers but selects the correct NaN payload and sign."}}
